meta {
  name: tag: phoenix-client (jupyter otel)
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/phoenix-client/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "pod_definition": {
      "description": "JupyterLab pre-wired to send OpenTelemetry/OpenInference traces to a self-hosted Arize Phoenix. Set PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT to your Phoenix pod, then instrument your LLM code in a notebook.",
      "image": "quay.io/jupyter/scipy-notebook:latest",
      "arguments": ["--IdentityProvider.token="],
      "secret_map": {
        "PHOENIX_API_KEY": "${pods:default::?Phoenix API key - only needed if the Phoenix pod has PHOENIX_ENABLE_AUTH=True. Leave blank otherwise.}"
      },
      "environment_variables": {
        "PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT": "${:?Phoenix collector base URL. In-cluster: http://pods-<site>-<tenant>-<phoenixPodId>:6006  |  External (needs a Tapis JWT): https://<phoenixPodId>.pods.<base>}",
        "PHOENIX_CLIENT_HEADERS": "authorization=Bearer ${pods:secrets:PHOENIX_API_KEY}",
        "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT": "${:?Same Phoenix host with the OTLP path, e.g. http://pods-<site>-<tenant>-<phoenixPodId>:6006/v1/traces}"
      },
      "networking": {
        "default": {
          "protocol": "http",
          "port": 8888,
          "tapis_auth": true,
          "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"],
          "tapis_auth_return_path": "/lab",
          "tapis_ui_uri_redirect": true,
          "tapis_ui_uri_description": "JupyterLab - instrument LLM code and watch traces land in Phoenix"
        }
      },
      "resources": { "cpu_request": 500, "cpu_limit": 2000, "mem_request": 512, "mem_limit": 4096 },
      "time_to_stop_default": -1
    },
    "tag": "jupyter-otel",
    "commit_message": "JupyterLab client preset with PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT for sending OpenInference traces to a self-hosted Phoenix; jupyter token disabled (tapis-auth gates the UI)."
  }
}

docs {
  ## A pod that *sends* traces to your self-hosted Phoenix

  This is the consumer side of `Create stack template tag (phoenix arize)`. It's a JupyterLab pod
  with the Phoenix collector env vars pre-declared, so you only fill in *where your Phoenix lives*
  and start instrumenting.

  ### Connecting to Phoenix - the one decision: which endpoint?
  Phoenix listens on **6006** (OTLP-HTTP + UI) and **4317** (OTLP-gRPC). Two ways to reach it:

  | From | Endpoint to use | Auth |
  |------|-----------------|------|
  | **Same cluster** (recommended) | `http://pods-<site>-<tenant>-<phoenixPodId>:6006` | none - in-cluster traffic |
  | **External / cross-tenant** | `https://<phoenixPodId>.pods.<base>` | the request must carry a **Tapis JWT** (tapis-auth gates it), which OTEL exporters don't send by default - prefer the in-cluster URL |

  Fill `PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT` (Phoenix client lib) and `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT`
  (raw OTEL exporters) with the same host - the former wants the **base** URL, the latter wants the
  base + `/v1/traces`.

  ### Instrument in a notebook
  ```python
  # one-time install in the notebook
  %pip install arize-phoenix-otel openinference-instrumentation-openai openai

  from phoenix.otel import register
  # reads PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT (and PHOENIX_CLIENT_HEADERS if auth is on) from the env
  tracer_provider = register(project_name="my-llm-app", auto_instrument=True)

  # now any instrumented client is traced automatically:
  from openai import OpenAI
  client = OpenAI()
  client.chat.completions.create(
      model="gpt-4o-mini",
      messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "hello phoenix"}],
  )
  # -> open the Phoenix UI; the span shows up under project "my-llm-app"
  ```
  `auto_instrument=True` picks up every `openinference-instrumentation-*` package you've installed
  (OpenAI, LangChain, LlamaIndex, Anthropic, Bedrock, ...). Install the ones matching your stack.

  ### If your Phoenix has auth on (`PHOENIX_ENABLE_AUTH=True`)
  Create an API key in the Phoenix UI and pass it as the `PHOENIX_API_KEY` secret when you
  instantiate this pod. `PHOENIX_CLIENT_HEADERS` is already templated to
  `authorization=Bearer <key>`; if auth is **off**, leave the key blank and the header is harmless.

  ### Instantiate
  `POST /pods` with `{ "template": "phoenix-client:jupyter-otel", "pod_id": "myphoenixclient",
  "template_overrides": { "secret_map": { ... }, "environment_variables": {
  "PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT": "http://pods-<site>-<tenant>-myphoenix:6006",
  "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT": "http://pods-<site>-<tenant>-myphoenix:6006/v1/traces" } } }`.

  > Jupyter's own token is disabled (`--IdentityProvider.token=`) because tapis-auth already gates
  > the pod URL. Don't expose this pod with `tapis_auth: false`.
}
